s row after the launch). FIRST RUN, EXERCISED. The three sights were served: defender_served holds S-32, S-266 and S-1822. The Oracle used G3856 (paradeigmatizo) in all four of its rounds (2, 2, 6 and 3 times) and G1165 in none, with Mark 7:7, 7:8, 7:9, Colossians 2:8, Hebrews 6:6 and G2977 in every round. No seat broke the Oracle on Matthew 1:19: sol and sonnet graded D3 against C3 UNDERDETERMINED; sol62 broke D3 on Matthew 1:18, not 1:19, and marked the challenger's own answer on 1:19 MISSES. Sol's limit on the ground: "Mark 7:8 supplies the category of human tradition but not the additional identification of this pregnancy's reproach with that category". The quotes were checked by W1 (Wall 12770). NOT SHOWN: a counted verdict; whether the notes field of Sight 32 is served. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks; objective_met stays 'in part' and status stays 'read back' until the second.$t$,
